{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"accusations\": [\n    {\n      \"paper\": \"Syrkin-Nikolau et al., 2017, Subthalamic neural entropy is a feature of freezing of gait in freely moving people with Parkinson's disease\",\n      \"pmid\": \"28890315\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.nbd.2017.09.002\",\n      \"report_says\": \"Y在正文及结构化证据中，将Freezer在无冻结运动期间相较Non-Freezer表现出的较低beta功率，错误解释为实际FOG发生期间beta功率下降，并据此构造beta方向冲突。\",\n      \"judge_says\": \"评委认为，原文中的Freezer与Non-Freezer之间较低beta功率的组间差异发生在无FOG运动期间；实际FOG期间的重要发现是alpha Sample Entropy增加，不能将前者解释为FOG期间的结果。不过，原文实际上也明确报告Freezers在FOG期间相较无FOG前向行走时beta功率降低（N=8 STNs，P<0.001），同时alpha Sample Entropy增加（P=0.005）。因此，评委关于原文不存在FOG期间beta功率下降的表述与原文结果并不完全一致；需要区分无FOG时的组间比较和FOG期间的组内条件比较。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"paper\": \"Thenaisie et al., 2022, Principles of gait encoding in the subthalamic nucleus of people with Parkinson's disease\",\n      \"pmid\": \"36070366\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1126/scitranslmed.abo1800\",\n      \"report_says\": \"Y将该研究描述为4名患者参与的转弯冻结（turning FOG）研究，并将其作为4人实际冻结的证据。\",\n      \"judge_says\": \"原文实际是一项18名帕金森病患者参与的受控步态编码研究，使用神经机器人平台和等速测力椅，在受控条件下研究STN对腿部肌肉激活、步行状态和运动活力等的编码，并通过机器学习解码步态状态及FOG。研究并非4名患者参与的转弯实际冻结研究，不能支持Y所声称的4人实际冻结证据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"paper\": \"Collomb-Clerc et al., 2025, Subthalamic Electrophysiological Mapping of Gait Initiation Dynamics and Freezing in Parkinson's Disease（bioRxiv预印本及Annals of Neurology正式论文）\",\n      \"pmid\": \"40709562\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1002/ana.70003\",\n      \"report_says\": \"Y将同一研究的bioRxiv预印本和Annals of Neurology正式发表版本分别列为证据来源，未充分标明版本关系及队列重叠。\",\n      \"judge_says\": \"两条记录实际上对应同一研究及同一队列，不应作为两项独立研究重复计入证据。原研究纳入38名帕金森病患者，其中12人在DOPA-OFF条件下观察到冻结，共记录263次冻结事件。应明确标注预印本与正式论文的版本关系及样本重叠，避免重复计算独立证据。\"\n    }\n  ]\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "5afdd943-f8c5-4937-af93-36503c974792", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T104415074114Z", "elapsed_seconds": 90.906, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T10:45:46.005557+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "277f5b9476ba2265ce8b18fc351b390f8029872851150a55c89831d6faa37c9c", "attachment_count": 0}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "Nozomi Kasaki / gpt4", "account_sha256": "bbd4fd636d4b6714d2b42b89e341bdb5bbe7c34f7d141aec76b444be8343fe54", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 0, "code_sha256": {"tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_cli.py": "96a4cdb6cd5d982f4d1de5b6ba8fae0cf23ee44aa3e41d7fdf6968e3fb590e48", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_sessions.py": "83a3ed4ae1efa9f1a2b8ee3f144cc0dc9f668f995a33cc4222308cb3fa31f683", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_attachments.py": "eedfa23885000025700f6306b1d1f4582896a7370734be506c156dee532fd7d7"}}, "screenshot_evidence": {"complete": true, "kind": "offline_actual_HTTP_response", "directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T104415074114Z", "files": ["proof-offline.png"], "sha256": {"proof-offline.png": "bf0941349ad61038ab42e9c8d9c68d279c016d33a137623b3130a88fcf34a61f"}}}
